  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the power of quotient rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{6}{{4}^{2}})}^{3}=\\frac{{6}^{3}}{{({4}^{2})}^{3}}\n$$\n\nTo simplify the denominator, we use the power rule for exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{6}^{3}}{{({4}^{2})}^{3}} & =\\frac{{6}^{3}}{{4}^{2\\cdot 3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{3}}{{4}^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
